# Keep the build context small and keep secrets out of images.
#
# Without this the context was 742MB, dominated by .venv and node_modules --
# both of which are rebuilt inside the image anyway. More importantly, a
# permissive context means a stray .env or key file can be copied into a layer,
# where deleting it in a later layer does not remove it.

.git
.gitignore

# Secrets -- never into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Rebuilt inside the image
.venv/
venv/
**/node_modules/
apps/web/.next/

# Build and test artefacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# Not needed at runtime
tests/
docs/
infrastructure/
.github/
*.md
!README.md
